-- title:
--   Distinct minimal primes over p on the pole chart
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and $M \ge 1$ with $p \mid M$ and $p^2 \nmid M$, a subgroup $H \le (\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$ containing every unit $u$ with trivial image under the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/(M/p))^\times$, and a witness `hj` that $j$-expansion series `jqModC ℚ` lies in the field `qExpFunctionFieldC ℚ ⊤`. Let `X p (ΓM M H) hj` and `X p (ΓN p M H hpM) hj` be the two-chart integral models over `Spec (R p)`, whose charts are the integral closures `chartAlgFin` of `R p`-adjoined $j$ and `chartAlgInf` of $1/j$ inside the respective $q$-expansion function fields, with chart immersions `ιFin`, `ιInf`. Given: a morphism $\pi$ of models over `Spec (R p)`; an `R p`-algebra map `iota0` between the $j$-finite chart rings which is the identity on underlying Laurent series, compatible with $\pi$ via `pi_chart`; a self-isomorphism $w$ of the level-`ΓM` model over the base together with an `R p`-algebra automorphism $\theta$ of its $j$-finite chart ring satisfying $\theta(\mathrm{iota0}\,b) = b(q^p)$, i.e. `qExpand ℚ p` applied to the series of $b$; a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $p$ a non-unit in $A$, residue field $\kappa$ algebraically closed of characteristic $p$, and a ring map $\rho : R p \to A$ lifting the structure map to $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, so that $\kappa$ becomes an `R p`-algebra; and two morphisms $\mathrm{comp}_0, \mathrm{comp}_1$ from the $\kappa$-fibre of the level-`ΓN` model to the $\kappa$-fibre of the level-`ΓM` model, each over the base, each a closed immersion, with $\mathrm{comp}_0$ a section of the fibre map of $\pi$ and $\mathrm{comp}_1 = \mathrm{comp}_0$ followed by the fibre map of $w$. The conclusion asserts: for every chart morphism $c_0$ from $\operatorname{Spec}(\kappa \otimes_{R p} \mathrm{chartAlgFin}(\Gamma_N))$ to the level-`ΓN` fibre whose two pullback projections are the expected ones (right inclusion followed by `ιFin`, and left inclusion), every such $c$ at level `ΓM` which moreover intertwines the fibre map of $w$ with $\operatorname{Spec}$ of $\mathrm{id}_\kappa \otimes \theta$, and every chart morphism $c'$ from $\operatorname{Spec}(\kappa \otimes_{R p} \mathrm{chartAlgInf}(\Gamma_M))$ to the level-`ΓM` fibre with the analogous compatibilities through `ιInf`, there are two distinct ideals $P_0, P_1$ of $\mathrm{chartAlgInf}(\Gamma_M)$, each a minimal prime of the ideal generated by $p$, such that for $i \in \{0,1\}$ and every point $z$ of $\operatorname{Spec}(\kappa \otimes_{R p} \mathrm{chartAlgInf}(\Gamma_M))$ with $c'(z)$ in the image of $\mathrm{comp}_i$, the ideal generated by the image of $P_i$ under the right inclusion is contained in the prime of $z$.
--
--   This is the separation statement for the two components of the mod-$p$ fibre of the two-chart integral model of $X_H(M)$ when $p$ exactly divides $M$: read on the pole chart (the integral closure of $1/j$), the identity copy and its Atkin–Lehner translate of the lower-level fibre lie over two different minimal primes of $(p)$, in the spirit of the Deligne–Rapoport and Katz–Mazur description of the fibre at $p$. It feeds the chart-level analysis of the Atkin–Lehner involution used in [`ModularCurve.XHDRLevel.fst_fst_pullback_comp_mem_range_iotaFin_and_fst_snd_pullback_comp_mem_range_iotaFin_of_chart_atkinLehner`](thm.html#ModularCurve.XHDRLevel.fst_fst_pullback_comp_mem_range_iotaFin_and_fst_snd_pullback_comp_mem_range_iotaFin_of_chart_atkinLehner).
